 "summary": "Lesson 10 teaches polite requests: [item] をください and [item] をおねがいします. The particle も adds ‘too / also’; でも means ‘but’. Ask なにがいいですか to find out what someone would like, and recognize service phrases such as いらっしゃいませ, どうぞ, and しょうしょうおまちください. Sizes such as エス, エム, and エル modify food names through の. Compound hiragana use a small や, ゆ, or よ after a kana, as in きゃ (kya), しゅ (shu), and ちょ (cho)."
